  "title": "O Little Town of Bethlehem",
  "composer": "Lewis Redner",
  "about": "Phillips Brooks, an Episcopal priest in Philadelphia, wrote the words in 1868 for his church. A visit to the village of Bethlehem three years before had inspired him. His organist, Lewis Redner, wrote this tune for it, called St. Louis. The United States and Canada sing the carol to this tune, and the United Kingdom and Ireland sing it to another.",
  "funFact": "Redner said he woke in the night hearing an angel-strain whispering in his ear, and jotted the tune down.",
